Description: glx: a stereo window whose two eyes the X server copies is shown flat, and the person is told
 A stereo window that stays one eye wide (declaration version 4) presents
 both eyes in one pixmap twice its width.  The X server hands that pixmap to
 the compositor whole, or copies it into the window, which keeps the left eye
 only; under the stereo declaration the compositor then shows half of the
 left view to each eye, and nothing told anyone.  PresentCompleteNotify says
 which happened (Present extension, PresentCompleteModeFlip and
 PresentCompleteModeCopy).
 .
 GLX now reads it, on DRI3 and on the software path (which selects Present
 events for a stereo window).  Two presents in a row of the window's own size
 that complete as copies take the declaration back: the properties are
 deleted, the window leaves its owner's list of stereo children, and from the
 next frame the left view alone is presented at the window's size (the
 program goes on drawing both).  One copy is not enough: a frame the server
 drops while the window manager unmaps and maps the window completes as a
 copy too.  A swap waits for its own completion until one pair was flipped
 and whenever the program's last swap is more than a tenth of a second old,
 and presents the same pair once more after a first copy, so a program that
 draws one frame is not left with the wrong picture.  While flat, three
 flips in a row of the left view bring the declaration back; when the pair is
 copied at once after two such returns, nothing more is tried at that size.
 LIBGL_DEBUG=verbose prints each completion until a pair is flipped.
 .
 The person is told through the distribution's place for failures: with the
 meson option sparky-stereo-problems-library (empty by default: the message
 goes to the log only) the problem is kept by sparky-stereo-problems under
 the package libglx-mesa0 with the key stereo-pair:PROGRAM, and ended when a
 pair is flipped again.  The library is opened at run time and never linked;
 a process that cannot load it (a 32-bit program) runs the engine's command.
 .
 MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=zink on an X server without DRI3 (Xwayland
 without glamor) ended GLX initialisation with "DRI3 not available", so every
 OpenGL program of a session that sets it for the whole desktop got no
 configuration.  Such a screen now takes the software renderer, as with any
 other driver on that server, and the person is told (key zink-without-dri3,
 ended by the next program that finds zink with DRI3).
